SEG = "STO"
CAT = "fnswStorage"
Q = [
    ("Under s 40, which material may an approved receptacle for category A or B firearms be made of?",
     "Hard wood", ["Chipboard", "Aluminium sheet", "Moulded plastic"],
     "Section 40(1)(a) requires a locked receptacle of an approved type, constructed of hard wood or steel and not easily penetrable."),
    ("Under s 40, the locks on a category A or B receptacle must be:",
     "Of solid metal", ["Of hardened plastic", "Combination dials only", "Any padlock at all"],
     "Section 40(1)(c) says the locks must be of solid metal and of a type approved by the Commissioner."),
    ("An empty gun cabinet for a category B rifle weighs 90 kg. Under s 40 it must be:",
     "Fixed to prevent easy removal", ["Inspected and weighed by police", "Kept in a locked garage", "Painted a plain colour"],
     "Section 40(1)(b) requires a receptacle weighing less than 150 kg when empty to be fixed so that it cannot easily be removed."),
    ("May ammunition be kept in the same locked receptacle as a category A rifle?",
     "No, it needs its own locked box", ["Yes, if it is on the top shelf", "Yes, if the bolt is taken out", "Yes, if the safe is bolted down"],
     "Section 40(1)(d) requires ammunition to be stored in a locked container of an approved type that is kept separate from the receptacle holding the firearm."),
    ("A primary producer's category C shotgun must be stored in:",
     "A bolted, locked steel safe", ["A locked hard wood cabinet", "A locked steel ute toolbox", "A locked and alarmed tool shed"],
     "Section 41 requires category C, D and H firearms to be stored in a locked, approved steel safe that cannot easily be penetrated and is bolted to the structure of the premises."),
    ("The steel safe rule in s 41 applies to firearms in which licence categories?",
     "Categories C, D and H", ["Every licence category", "Air rifles only", "Only category H pistols"],
     "Section 41 covers category C, D and H licences. Category A and B firearms may instead be kept in a locked hard wood or steel receptacle under s 40."),
    ("A licensee wants to use storage that differs from the s 40 rules. The Commissioner can accept it if it is:",
     "At least as secure", ["Cheaper to install", "Approved by a club", "Kept off the premises"],
     "Section 40(2) excuses compliance if the licensee satisfies the Commissioner that the alternative arrangements are of a standard not less than the s 40 requirements."),
    ("Under s 39, everyone who possesses a firearm must take all reasonable precautions so that it:",
     "Is not lost or stolen", ["Is cleaned every month", "Is kept at the club", "Is insured for theft"],
     "Section 39(1) requires all reasonable precautions for the firearm's safe keeping, that it is not stolen or lost and that it does not come into the possession of an unauthorised person."),
    ("A police officer reasonably believes your rifle is not kept as Part 4 requires. Under s 42 the officer must:",
     "Seize it unless fixed without delay", ["Issue you a written warning only", "Notify your club", "Book a later inspection"],
     "Section 42 requires seizure of a firearm or ammunition not kept as required, unless the officer is satisfied the failure has been, or will without delay be, rectified."),
    ("Police leave your rifle with you because a storage failure was fixed on the spot. You:",
     "Can still be prosecuted", ["Can no longer be fined for it", "Must sell the rifle", "Lose your licence"],
     "Section 42(2) says a decision not to seize because the failure was rectified does not prevent a prosecution or a penalty notice for the failure."),
    ("The Commissioner will not issue a licence unless satisfied the applicant can meet:",
     "The Part 4 storage rules", ["A minimum income test", "A physical fitness test", "A marksmanship standard"],
     "Section 11(3)(c) requires the Commissioner to be satisfied that the storage and safety requirements in Part 4 are capable of being met by the applicant."),
    ("When must a category A rifle be locked in its receptacle under s 40?",
     "When not being used or carried", ["Only overnight and when away", "Only when visitors are in the house", "Only between seasons"],
     "Section 40(1)(a) applies whenever the firearm is not actually being used or carried, not just at night or when others are present."),
    ("To make a firearm temporarily unable to fire for a car trip, the NSW Police users guide suggests:",
     "Bolt out or a trigger lock", ["Taping over the muzzle end", "Loosening the scope", "Removing the sling"],
     "The NSW Police Firearms (Longarms) Users Guide says to make sure the firearm is unloaded and to remove the bolt or fit a trigger lock or other commercial device."),
    ("A cased rifle will not fit in the car boot. The NSW Police users guide says to:",
     "Cover it and lock the car", ["Lay it openly on the back seat", "Prop it by the door", "Leave a window open"],
     "The users guide says to lock the firearm out of sight, such as in the boot, and if it will not fit, to cover it from view and lock the vehicle."),
    ("When travelling with a firearm, the NSW Police users guide suggests keeping the ammunition:",
     "In a locked glove box", ["In the rifle's magazine", "Loose in the boot", "In a jacket pocket"],
     "The users guide says ammunition must be locked in a separate container inside the vehicle, for example in the locked glove box."),
    ("A business that transports goods for others may carry a firearm only:",
     "Under prescribed safety rules", ["With a police escort the whole way", "During daylight hours", "If the owner is a licensed dealer"],
     "Section 56 says a person in the business of transporting goods must not transport a firearm unless it is conveyed in accordance with the safety requirements prescribed by the regulations."),
    ("The National Firearms Safety Code says that when storing a firearm you should never:",
     "Block the barrel", ["Oil it lightly", "Clean the bore", "Remove the magazine"],
     "The Code says never block the barrel when storing a firearm; make sure the barrel is clean and coat the firearm lightly with oil."),
    ("According to the National Firearms Safety Code, a parked vehicle is:",
     "Not a secure store", ["Secure if the doors lock", "Secure if out of sight", "Secure for one night"],
     "The Code says vehicles should not be considered a secure option for storing firearms, even when cases are kept out of sight."),
    ("The National Firearms Safety Code says many firearm incidents in the home happen because:",
     "They are stored with ammunition", ["Safes are too heavy to move alone", "Cleaning kits are left out", "Bolts go missing"],
     "The Code says many incidents occur because firearms and ammunition are stored together, and children's curiosity makes this especially dangerous."),
    ("Before storing a bolt action rifle, the National Firearms Safety Code says that, if possible, you should:",
     "Lock the bolt away separately", ["Leave a round in the chamber", "Close and cock the bolt", "Tape over the trigger guard"],
     "The Code says to make sure the magazine and chamber are empty, clean the firearm, and if possible remove the bolt and magazine and lock them away separately from the firearm."),
]
